Treat CMake's QCC compiler like GCC.

CMake identifies QNX's qcc as "QCC", not "GNU", so gnu.cmake was skipped:
no -fvisibility=hidden (every module then exports all its symbols, and the
engine and game modules interpose each other's), no -fno-strict-aliasing
(the code relies on union type punning), and no ftola/snapvector sources.

Upstream-Status: Pending

diff --git a/cmake/compilers/gnu.cmake b/cmake/compilers/gnu.cmake
--- a/cmake/compilers/gnu.cmake
+++ b/cmake/compilers/gnu.cmake
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 # GNU style (GCC/Clang) compiler specific settings
 
-if(NOT CMAKE_C_COMPILER_ID STREQUAL "GNU" AND NOT CMAKE_C_COMPILER_ID MATCHES "^(Apple)?Clang$")
+# QNX's qcc is GCC behind a driver; CMake calls it QCC.
+if(NOT CMAKE_C_COMPILER_ID STREQUAL "GNU" AND NOT CMAKE_C_COMPILER_ID STREQUAL "QCC" AND NOT CMAKE_C_COMPILER_ID MATCHES "^(Apple)?Clang$")
     return()
 endif()
 
